id: pm-f7shxf
title: Invalidate shared history projections when writers lack SQLite
description: A SQLite-less append followed by a Node indexed append can certify a projection with a current stream-size receipt while omitting the middle authoritative fact. The history stream retains all three entries. Every supported runtime must participate in the invalidation protocol so a later indexed writer cannot hide earlier facts.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-17T22:34:40.375Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-17T23:06:11.479Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-17T23:06:10.560Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-17T23:06:10.560Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce two projected facts versus three authoritative facts before the fix; Preserve all three facts after a later indexed append; Exercise real Bun and Node against one isolated tracker; Keep cursor and return shapes compatible; Retain portable committed invalidation and full-source quality gates
goal: project management = context management
objective: Preserve complete shared-workspace mutation facts across SQLite and non-SQLite producers
value: Bun and Node can safely share the same project context without silent event omissions
why_now: The second review concurrency controls independently reproduced a missing middle event in a three-append mixed-backend sequence.
parent: pm-lvyd
risk: medium
confidence: 95
resolution: "Route every non-indexed authoritative append through the existing pending/committed invalidation protocol so later indexed writers cannot certify an incomplete projection. Preserve portable fallback, typed failures and existing event shapes."
expected_result: "A SQLite-less middle append between two indexed appends remains visible as a complete fact, and optional repair restores all stream offsets without loss or duplication."
actual_result: Negative control reproduced two cached facts versus three authoritative facts before the fix; the linked omitted-fact regression now passes. Real public-SDK Node26.9.0/Bun1.4.3 shared-tracker acceptance returns three unique full update facts exactly matching authoritative history and passes strict drift validation. Current Bun exposes SQLite; forced constructor unavailability separately validates the supported SQLite-less path. Full final static pipeline and four typechecks pass; final-head hosted full coverage remains required.
